      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Wkly Epidem. Rec.: Mo. 43 - 27 Oct 197g\nRelevé epidem, hebd.' N° 43 - 27 OCL 197g\nThree meningococcal polysaccharide vaccines, monovalent A, \nmonovalent C, and bivalent A-C vaccine,* are licensed for selective \nuse in the United States. These vaccines are chemically defined \nantigens consisting of purified bacterial capsular polysaccharide, \neach inducing specific serogroup immunity. The duration of \nimmunity conferred by each vaccine is unknown.\nSerogroup A vaccine was evaluated in 62 000 Egyptian school- \nchildren 6-15 years old and appeared to be highly effective and not \nto induce any seri",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the meningococcal vaccine statement, describing the monovalent A, monovalent C and bivalent vaccines, evidence of effectiveness from Egypt and Brazil, and poor effectiveness of serogroup C vaccine under two years. It advises against routine civilian vaccination but recommends use in serogroup A or C outbreaks, for some travellers and as an adjunct for household contacts, noting mild side effects and caution in pregnancy. A French version and notes on polyvalent vaccine development follow.",
